    <content>
      <Value><![CDATA[# My First Razor Render

Writing C# and Razor templates is an exercise in logic. When I compiled my first view, I had to ensure all imports like `@inherits` were correct and that I retrieved values safely using `Model.Value()`.

## What I Learned
- **Tiptap vs standard text:** Rich text content stored via the Tiptap editor requires rendering raw HTML string: `@Html.Raw(Model.Value("bodyText"))`.
- **Markdown conversion:** Umbraco is amazingly clever; it converts markdown strings automatically into clean HTML, which I can render directly.
- **Layout reuse:** By centralizing styles and structural shell in `_Layout.cshtml`, I can keep individual template files clean and light.

Next up, I will be adding dynamic navigation and an elegant visual flow!]]></Value>
    </content>
